Browser driving, as a shipped skill
===================================

Upstream ships a browser PANE - tabs, URLs and titles in the UI - but nothing that tells the agent how
to drive a real browser. That knowledge lived outside, which meant a fresh install had no idea how to
get past a wall.

This ships it as a skill, through the same mechanism as the rest of the bundled set.

The content is the operational core, not theory:

  * Which engine takes which driver. Firefox has had no CDP since 129 - it is WebDriver BiDi now, and
    anything describing CDP-for-Firefox is describing a browser that no longer exists.
  * Brave/Chromium over `--remote-debugging-port`, with the HTTP endpoints and a WebSocket attach.
  * The three mistakes that cost real time: port 9222 is usually the user's own browser, a relaunch on
    the same `--user-data-dir` is silently ignored, and native Wayland windows are invisible to
    xdotool.
  * Passing a wall: a real profile the site already trusts beats fingerprint spoofing every time.
  * curl as the fallback, with the false negative spelled out - a helper that discards the HTTP status
    reports a 429 or a 202 challenge as "zero results", which is indistinguishable from a genuinely
    empty page unless you check the code.

Every CDP endpoint named here was exercised before shipping:
  GET  /json/version   -> HTTP 200
  GET  /json/list      -> HTTP 200
  PUT  /json/new?...   -> HTTP 200

